What is the output of the following Java program?

```java
interface Shape { double area(); }

class Square implements Shape {
    public double area() { return 4; }
}
class Circle implements Shape {
    public double area() { return 3; }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Shape[] shapes = { new Square(), new Circle(), new Square() };
        double total = 0;
        for (Shape s : shapes) total += s.area();
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program?

```java
class Counter {
    static int s = 0;
    int i = 0;
    Counter() { s++; i++; }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Counter a = new Counter();
        Counter b = new Counter();
        Counter c = new Counter();
        System.out.println(a.i + " " + c.s);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program?

```java
class Printer {
    void show(Object o) { System.out.println("Object"); }
    void show(String s) { System.out.println("String"); }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Printer p = new Printer();
        Object x = "hello";
        p.show(x);
        p.show("hi");
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program?

```java
class A {
    void f(Object o) { System.out.println("A-Object"); }
}
class B extends A {
    @Override
    void f(Object o) { System.out.println("B-Object"); }
    void f(String s) { System.out.println("B-String"); }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        A ref = new B();
        ref.f("hi");
    }
}
```
